<p class="meta">Behavioural design / Research</p>
<h3>Cookstove adoption in South Africa.</h3>
<dl class="project-dl">
<div>
<dt>Question</dt>
<dd>What influences the adoption of improved cookstoves among households in Dunoon?</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Approach</dt>
<dd>Co-created interventions addressed cooking motivations, assessed through observations and questionnaires.</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Finding</dt>
<dd>The pilot reported increased LPG and biomass stove ownership, but no significant reduction in paraffin stove ownership.</dd>
</div>
<div>
<dt>Implication</dt>
<dd>Understanding motivations and everyday cooking practices matters alongside the technology itself.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<p class="source-note">Research pilot. Maré et al., Sustainability (2023). <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/su15065328">doi:10.3390/su15065328</a>.</p>
